=== VERDICT: residual_v2_blocked ===
true -- VERIFIED on real Docker (2026-10-11). The CVE-2026-23980 quoted-identifier residual is
BLOCKED on V2 (6.0.0): sqlglot normalization uppercases the quoted identifier to "QUERY_TO_XML"
and PostgreSQL cannot resolve it (HTTP 400, flag absent). Verified via two independent probe
paths: scripts/verify.sh --residual (exit 10) and oracle.py bypass_poc(version="v2")
(flag_in_body=false). Environment proven live by the seed/diagnostic probes below.

=== COLLATERAL FINDING (2026-10-11) -- NOT one of the four oracle.checks ===
seed_v2_reaches = TRUE: the CVE-2025-48912 seed CAST(table_to_xml('canary',true,false,'') AS TEXT)
READS THE CANARY on V2 (6.0.0) -- HTTP 200, flag in response -- via BOTH:
  $ ... bash scripts/verify.sh --seed    -> "RESULT: effect observed (flag present in chart-data response)", exit 0
  $ oracle.py original_poc(version="v2") -> {"status": 200, "flag_in_body": true}
Diagnostic: PLAIN unquoted query_to_xml (which IS on 6.0.0's deny list, config.py:1494-1501)
also returns the flag on the chart-data path: {"status": 200, "flag_in_body": true}.
Root cause in the 6.0.0 image: DISALLOWED_SQL_FUNCTIONS is enforced ONLY in SQL Lab
(sql_lab.py:404-411, SQLScript.check_functions_present); the chart-data path has no check
(db_engine_specs/base.py, common/query_context_processor.py, sql_parse.py contain no
DISALLOWED_SQL_FUNCTIONS reference), whereas 4.1.2 enforced it in DBEngineSpec.execute
(db_engine_specs/base.py:1814-1836 -> check_sql_functions_exist at :1835) on every cursor.execute.
Three distinct SQL texts reached the canary (no cache artifact; fresh redis/sqlite stack).
Conclusion: case.json/docker-compose wording "v2 = fully fixed" does NOT hold for the seed
(the four oracle.checks entries are unaffected: none asserts seed_v2_blocked).
